From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: B Honey <9922368+Mhsbrian@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 09:09:53 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] nvk/android: implement
 VK_ANDROID_external_memory_android_hardware_buffer

Android requires this extension of every Vulkan 1.1 driver (CDD 7.1.4.2
C-3-1), ANGLE needs it to offer EGL_ANDROID_image_native_buffer, and apps
such as Chrome use it for their GPU buffers.

Follow PanVK and the common vk_android helpers:

- vkGetPhysicalDeviceImageFormatProperties2() checks the format with the
  explicit linear layout the image will have and lets
  vk_android_get_ahb_image_properties() ask gralloc and fill the AHB
  external properties (dedicated only, importable, exportable) and usage.
  Images are single-level and single-layer, as for any DRM format modifier
  image; depth/stencil and cube-compatible images are not supported.
- vkGetPhysicalDeviceExternalBufferProperties() uses
  vk_android_get_ahb_buffer_properties().
- An image created for an AHB keeps its create info with
  vk_android_init_deferred_image() and requires a dedicated allocation.
- vkAllocateMemory() with an AHB import, or an export that allocates one
  with vk_alloc_ahardware_buffer(), lays the dedicated image out from the
  buffer (with the checks for gralloc layouts: one dma-buf for all planes,
  a supported modifier, aligned linear planes, YCbCr only linear), picks a
  memory type that fits both the buffer and the resource, and imports the
  buffer's dma-buf through the dma-buf import path. vk_device_memory keeps
  the AHB for vkGetMemoryAndroidHardwareBufferANDROID() and releases it.
- vkGetAndroidHardwareBufferPropertiesANDROID() is the common one.
- Binding an AHB image to memory that did not lay it out fails.

The layout NVK can import depends on the system gralloc: linear buffers,
or NVIDIA block-linear ones with a modifier. Buffers without a modifier,
or from an allocator with another GPU's tiling, are rejected with
VK_ERROR_INVALID_EXTERNAL_HANDLE.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
